{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772644237,"nonce":"edHgVlkkKlbHL6E8GkUT2AsLtWw=","title":"GRUOracle is redundant with GRU — remove from registry","message":"GRUOracle was registered as a named component likely as an artifact of bbooddyy experiments, but it provides no additional capability over a plain GRU: a GRU already maintains its own hidden state, so leaving the feedback port unconnected achieves the same thing. There is no Python class backing GRUOracle.\n\n## Recommendation\nRemove GRUOracle from the component registry. If the experimental distinction matters (e.g., \"this run used a GRU with no feedback\"), that should be represented as a GRU configuration or experiment note, not a separate component type.\n\n## Files\n- `feedbax/web/services/component_registry.py`: remove GRUOracle entry\n- Any serialization/deserialization references to GRUOracle","files":null}]}